  m_Name: 
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Assembly-CSharp::ComputerInteractable
  computerName: Frank's Ofiice computer
  categories:
  - categoryName: Case Studies
    isUnlocked: 0
    entries:
    - title: '2026 '
      image: {fileID: 0}
      audio: {fileID: 0}
      text: dgecyjdg
  - categoryName: 'Case Files '
    isUnlocked: 1
    entries:
    - title: 'Police report '
      image: {fileID: 21300000, guid: 85622a530d3f9e044bece05b21119254, type: 3}
      audio: {fileID: 0}
      text: '

        Senior Detective Frank Clifton

        Year: 2028



        Case:Witnessed
        Murder

        Location:Sector 7, New Avalon City

        Date:14 October
        2028



        At approximately 22:40, I responded to a reported murder
        in Sector 7. Upon arrival, I found the victim, identified as Elias Vance,
        deceased in an alleyway.



        A civilian witness stated that they saw
        the victim arguing with an unidentified individual shortly before the attack.
        The suspect appeared to have several visible cybernetic implants but concealed
        their face with a hood.



        The witness reported seeing the suspect
        place a hand against the victim''s chest before the victim suddenly collapsed.
        No conventional weapon was found at the scene.



        The area has been
        secured and the victim''s cybernetic systems have been taken for forensic
        examination.



        Senior Detective Frank Clifton



'
    - title: 'Police report '
      image: {fileID: 21300000, guid: 85622a530d3f9e044bece05b21119254, type: 3}
      audio: {fileID: 0}
      text: '

        Senior Detective Frank Clifton

        Year: 2028



        Case:Kidnapping

        Location:Sector
        12, New Avalon City

        Date:18 October 2028



        At approximately
        19:15, I responded to a reported kidnapping at a residential apartment in
        Sector 12. The victim, identified as **Mara Voss**, was reported missing
        by a family member after failing to respond to multiple calls.



        Security
        footage shows the victim leaving the building with an unidentified individual.
        The suspect''s face was digitally obscured, suggesting the use of illegal
        cybernetic or visual-masking technology.



        Investigators found signs
        of forced entry and a damaged neural-interface device inside the victim''s
        apartment. No ransom demand has been received at this time.



        The
        victim''s cybernetic identification signal was last detected approximately
        three kilometres from the scene before going offline.



        The investigation
        remains active. The victim''s location and the identity of the suspect are
        currently unknown.



        Senior Detective Frank Clifton





'
  - categoryName: 'Emplyee Information '
    isUnlocked: 1
    entries:
    - title: 'Police report '
      image: {fileID: 21300000, guid: 85622a530d3f9e044bece05b21119254, type: 3}
      audio: {fileID: 0}
      text: "Name : Frank \nSurname : Cliffton\nJob Title: Senior detective \nHealth:
        Good\nImplant: HIGH RISK\r\n"
